  "settings": {
    "nativeConfiguration": "restricted"
  },
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "fixer-judge-task",
      "type": "text",
      "config": {
        "value": "FIXER TASK ADR6-PREFLIGHT-001\nJudge: the external Codex chat, GPT 6.1 Sol, effort=max. The Judge is not an Agent node.\nMode: read-only preflight. This first task authorizes no source edits or deployment.\nGoal: reconcile the actual remaining ADR-0006 engineering and identify ONE small unblocked implementation task for the Judge to assign next. Do not attempt the whole ADR in one invocation.\nRead docs/adr/0006-time-bounded-autonomy-and-application-lifecycle.md, docs/adr/0006-completion-plan.md, docs/adr/0006-implementation-status.md, docs/adr/0006-acceptance-matrix.md, and the latest .deszo/pilots/adr6-completion/CHECKPOINT*.md. Inspect the actual relevant source before claiming a gap still exists.\nAcceptance: provide exact file/criterion references, distinguish source/fixture/installed/actual-app evidence, identify the next bounded task and its check, and list real human dependencies separately. Return READY_FOR_REVIEW when the read-only report is ready.\nAllowed source writes: none. Allowed commands: bounded read-only local inspection only. Do not invoke provider CLIs, start runtimes, run builds, create policy, change installed files/services/tasks, or perform authentication/UI input.\nUse the configured workspace only. An isolated captured working copy must be selected before running; preserve all pre-existing dirty work. Report mismatches instead of fixing them.\nThe earlier diagnostic policy expired. It had used operations=10 and restarts=9; all model counters were zero. These are historical inputs, not current permission. The Judge must verify live authority and exact run supervision before dispatch.\nAfter this preflight the Judge assigns one implementation task at a time through a new captured task brief/revision or existing legal checkpoint mechanism. No task scope, model/effort, review rule, limit, or source reference changes implicitly.\nPush, merge, release, protected-host installation, and final ADR acceptance are outside this task. ADR-0003 through ADR-0005 remain subsequent separately assigned work; their independent review and acceptance requirements remain applicable."
      }
    },
    {
